{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740699-monster-plot-hooks","id":740699,"title":"Monster Plot Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-29T20:14:32-07:00","id":740699,"title":"Monster Plot Hooks","content":"As the title says, this thread is dedicated to plot hooks involving monsters both familiar and unfamiliar. One user suggests a monster to be used in a plot hook, and the next poster writes a prompt based on that monster. These prompts can be for adventures, character ideas, plot twists, and so forth. I'll start:<br /> <br /> <b>Asteria (Greek Star Nymph):</b><br /> <br /> All around town, 911 has been called to various sites of radiation poisoning and victims of what looks like nuclear spills. The local chemical company is everyone's first thought, as they've been dumping radioactive and toxic material into the local streams and forests for years. On top of the clashes between townsfolk and big business, UFO hunters are flocking towards the town, as strange lights have been seen in the sky around these radioactive areas; they aren't interested in portraying the town in a positive light. Between being shown as Hickville on national TV, and the growing environmental concerns, everyone is on edge.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a strange and cosmic being, baffled and only trying to defend herself from people trying to capture her, is searching for a way to join her sisters in the sky again. Curiosity brought her down to the mortal world, and now, she can't find her way home.<br /> <br /> Next monster: <b>Bigfoot</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:05:52-07:00","id":745539,"title":"","content":"&quot;You wanna know the real reason that it's so hard to catch a Bigfoot on camera, it's not because they're shy, it's because they can't tell the difference between a camera and a gun.<br /> It's like this, you know how certain Asian schools of &quot;alternative&quot; medicine use tiger dick as viagra and such? well the chinese also use Bigfoot teeth as medicine, no I don't know what they use it to try and treat!<br /> <br /> See the Triads come to America to hunt the Bigfeet, because the Tibetan population is running low. But there's one thing the Chinese don't know, the Predator Kings think the Bigfeet are &quot;blessed&quot; by Dire Wolf, apparently there were a bunch of humans who gave in enough to their animal nature that he changed their forms to match their unleashed inner ape and supposedly Dire Wolf occasionally &quot;replenishes&quot; the bigfoot population by turning suitable humans into those things.<br /> <br /> It seems a war is brewing between the Triads and the Predator kings over this and let me tell you, we do not want to be here when it starts.&quot;<br /> <br /> (this is actually two hooks for one, now that I think about it.)<br /> <br /> Next Monster: The Piasa Bird!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:21:58-07:00","id":745566,"title":"","content":"The Piasa is neither beast nor spirit, neither idigam nor shapeshifter. It is instead one of the few remaining flesh-gods of the Border Marches, sealed away in stone and dirt after a great clash with the <i>Uratha</i> of North America. So that everyone might forget the monstrosity that is the Piasa, its image was washed away by benevolent rain-spirits as part of a great ritual. Now that the Piasa's image is restored, the beast stirs and awakens, effortlessly passing to and fro over the Gauntlet as it begins devouring <i>Uratha</i> to take their rich essence. The wolfmen are the closest thing to a Border-god that remains in the <i>Gurihal</i>, and in order to strengthen itself after years of sleep and starvation, the Piasa must hunt down and eat as many as it can find.<br /> <br /> Next monster: <b>Hersinia</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:25:31-08:00","id":757813,"title":"","content":"Sikla, I think the reason nobody replied to that last monster is because even google doesn't know what it is. Seriously, I googled it and couldn't find it, which actually impressed me.<br /> <br /> So let me try something less obscure and see what people do with it<br /> <br /> <b>The Great Leech of Tlanusi'yi. </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}